                </command><command>
                        <name>Siemens.SimaticIT.UAPI.MasterData.CT_MS.MSModel.Commands.MigrateSBTaskDefinitionForRecipeDecoupling</name>
                        <shortname>MigrateSBTaskDefinitionForRecipeDecoupling</shortname>
                        <description>Updates the existing Batch Task Definition, adding the ParameterId and DataTypeId properties to each Task Definition Parameter. If you specify the Top value in input, the command retrieves and updates only a number of Task Definition Parameters up to the value you have inserted. This is intended for those use cases where the system resources may suffer due to the command execution on a large number of Task Definition Parameters. You can start by setting a value for the Top input field (for example 1000); upon each command execution, the output field NbToProcess will prompt the total number of Task Definition Parameters that require to be updated, thus letting you tune an appropriate value for the Top input parameter for subsequent command call, if required. Each time you call the command and a set of Task Definition Parameters is updated, the value for the output field NbToProcess will be lowered accordingly. The command: 1. Retrieves all the Batch Task Definition Parameters missing the ParameterId and DataTypeId properties; optionally, if you have specified a value for the Top input field, the maximum number of Batch Task Definition Parameters will be limited according to the value you have set. 2. Groups the Batch Task Definition Parameters by Master Recipe/Formula. 3. Retrieves the engineering data for each Master Recipe/Formula and uses the ParameterId and DataTypeId values to update the Batch Task Definition Parameters.</description>
                        <assembly>Siemens.SimaticIT.UAPI.MasterData.CT_MS.MSModel.Commands, Version=1.0.0.0, Culture=neutral, PublicKeyToken=null</assembly>
                        <dotnetcommandtype></dotnetcommandtype>
